		replace: "\treturn pwuTypeId;",
		expectRed: ["packages/rph-application/src/prompt-render.test.ts"],
		why: "Its docblock quotes the obligation directly: \"The identity `MODEL_EXCHANGE.promptTemplateFingerprint` finally resolves to. ⭑ `PER-9`: 'A prompt or template fingerprint identifies that record; it never substitutes for it.' Until `REG-D-058` the field fingerprinted a template with no home — an identifier for a thing that did not exist. It now names an owning type and a version, which is a thing a reader can go and look at.\" WHO RELIES: `prepareModelInvocation` (execution-invocation.ts:215) puts this string on `InvocationPlan.fingerprint`, which is what ends up recorded as `MODEL_EXCHANGE.promptTemplateFingerprint` — the identity an auditor uses to go back to the instruction a model was actually given. WHAT THE MUTATION DOES TO THEM: dropping the version leaves the fingerprint naming a type only, so two exchanges produced under different versions of the same type's template become indistinguishable to that auditor. The field reverts to identifying something a reader cannot go and look at — precisely the pre-REG-D-058 defect the docblock records as closed.\n\nOBSERVED: Anchor measured at line 90; `promptTemplateFingerprint` declaration spans lines 89-91. CLEAN: Tests 7 passed (7). MUTATED: Tests 1 failed | 6 passed (7); the single red is `the fingerprint names an owning type and a version — a thing a reader can go and look at` with `AssertionError: expected 'pwut_abc' to be 'pwut_abc@v3'` at prompt-render.test.ts:77. RESTORED by inverting the edit; sha256 back to the baseline d31a90a0…3dd52 and the suite re-run green at 7 passed (7).",
